# EVIDENCE REQUIREMENTS

Every major section must end with an **Evidence** subsection containing:

* Tests executed
* Commands or procedures used
* Input datasets or workloads
* Environment details
* Raw measurements
* Relevant logs
* Screenshots (where applicable)
* Metrics collected
* Files inspected
* Confidence level (High / Medium / Low)
* Limitations affecting interpretation

If evidence is incomplete, the report must explicitly identify the limitation instead of drawing unsupported conclusions.

---

# CERTIFICATION PRINCIPLES

The report is intended to serve as an enterprise-quality validation artifact.

It must withstand technical review, engineering scrutiny, procurement evaluation, executive decision-making, and future regression comparisons.

The report shall distinguish clearly between:

* Measured facts
* Observations
* Evidence
* Risks
* Assumptions
* Recommendations

No recommendation may be presented as an observed fact.

No observed fact may be presented without supporting evidence.

The completed document shall become the authoritative benchmark against which all future releases of the software are evaluated.
